d later B7 linker topology\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:855:Reference-by-hash is a stream process, not hidden VM machinery. B6 is the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:860:all IO and data flow through append-only streams. No global mutable registry\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:862:The boundary is `dao.stream`; local and remote resolution are the same\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:866:`dao.jing` stores and fetches the image as a value at its own content\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:867:address, over `dao.stream` through `dao.jing.remote`. B verifies the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:877:unavailable, the linked interpreter parks its explicit continuation and emits a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:882:loads only verified images, and resumes. The request token, parked\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:883:continuation, and response are data; no callback is retained. Gaps,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:884:timeouts, and permanent absence remain explicit stream events.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:889:value or stream with a declared ledger, trust, and provenance. Streams provide\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:893:loading and continuation state explicit, and B4 carries park and resume as\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:895:never invokes a loader; absence is a park plus a request emission.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:903:### 7.3 Lossless source view non-goal\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:916:## 8. Risks and owner decisions\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:925:   arity comparison, continuation and parked type comparison, stream/cursor\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:926:   ids, host-handle-free stores, and telemetry exclusion. This serves\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:934:   `:env` on return and park (`semantic.cljc:285-293, 317`); `vm-load-program`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:935:   does not reset it (`semantic.cljc:679-690`), while `vm-eval